WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.428 --> 00:00:01.484
- Good morning Believe Nation,

00:00:01.484 --> 00:00:04.859
today's message is do what you love.

00:00:04.859 --> 00:00:06.412
Over to you, Future.

00:00:06.412 --> 00:00:08.850
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.369
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.369 --> 00:00:14.205
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:14.205 --> 00:00:18.237
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.237 --> 00:00:21.479
- I'm most comfortable
when I'm in the studio,

00:00:21.479 --> 00:00:23.439
and nothing else matters but the music.

00:00:23.439 --> 00:00:24.976
You got this love for it,

00:00:24.976 --> 00:00:26.236
for something that you think about.

00:00:26.236 --> 00:00:28.186
You sleep and you dream and you wake up

00:00:28.186 --> 00:00:29.993
and you breathe it and
you want to live it.

00:00:29.993 --> 00:00:33.274
There's so many options,
there's many ways to blow up,

00:00:33.274 --> 00:00:34.900
there's many ways to be known

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.378
and to get success and to be successful.

00:00:37.378 --> 00:00:39.552
It's just about picking
that way that feeds you.

00:00:39.552 --> 00:00:42.060
- So here's the path for
so many successful people.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.604
You get an interest in something,

00:00:43.604 --> 00:00:45.749
you want to try something, so you try it.

00:00:45.749 --> 00:00:48.126
You suck at it, but you really enjoyed it

00:00:48.126 --> 00:00:49.881
so you come back and you do it again.

00:00:49.881 --> 00:00:51.516
And you try to get better and you improve.

00:00:51.516 --> 00:00:53.456
You come back, you suck a little bit less

00:00:53.456 --> 00:00:54.515
but you're still really bad,

00:00:54.515 --> 00:00:57.066
but you love it so much
you have to keep doing it.

00:00:57.066 --> 00:00:58.475
Even though it doesn't make sense,

00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:00.743
even though you're not
seeing any kind of return,

00:01:00.743 --> 00:01:02.230
you just love doing it.

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:04.058
Even though people are
telling you that you're crazy,

00:01:04.058 --> 00:01:06.129
even though your parents
or your friends are saying

00:01:06.129 --> 00:01:08.040
what the heck are you doing,
this doesn't make any sense

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:08.984
in the world.

00:01:08.984 --> 00:01:13.018
You have to keep doing it
because you love the process.

00:01:13.018 --> 00:01:14.937
And slowly here's what happens.

00:01:14.937 --> 00:01:17.233
You get a little bit better,
you get a little bit better,

00:01:17.233 --> 00:01:19.192
you work harder, you
get a little bit better.

00:01:19.192 --> 00:01:20.941
Now suddenly, you're average.

00:01:20.941 --> 00:01:23.238
You're just average, but
you're still spending time,

00:01:23.238 --> 00:01:24.213
you're still spending effort,

00:01:24.213 --> 00:01:25.949
you're still hustling
to try to get better.

00:01:25.949 --> 00:01:27.545
You still have the
people around you saying

00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:29.381
that you're crazy, that
you're never going to make it,

00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:30.825
that the numbers are against you.

00:01:30.825 --> 00:01:32.977
Why don't you do the smart,
safe, practical thing to do

00:01:32.977 --> 00:01:35.957
and go on that other route
instead of doing this thing?

00:01:35.957 --> 00:01:37.692
'Cause now you're just average.

00:01:37.692 --> 00:01:39.480
I got to keep doing it, I love it.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.402
So you do more, you practice harder,

00:01:41.402 --> 00:01:44.519
you hustle, you hustle, you
hustle, you grind it more.

00:01:44.519 --> 00:01:46.815
Now you're good, now you're good.

00:01:46.815 --> 00:01:49.304
Now maybe you've made even a
little bit of money off of it,

00:01:49.304 --> 00:01:51.235
whatever this hobby,
passion thing is of yours.

00:01:51.235 --> 00:01:52.556
And you still got the people saying

00:01:52.556 --> 00:01:54.202
you're never going to make it.

00:01:54.202 --> 00:01:55.915
You're just making a little bit of money,

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.660
how are you ever going to
turn that thing into a career?

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.123
It's never going to happen for you.

00:02:00.123 --> 00:02:00.956
There's no way.

00:02:00.956 --> 00:02:02.825
Look at all these
massively talented people

00:02:02.825 --> 00:02:03.690
who are ahead of you.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.518
You think you're going to
compete with those guys?

00:02:05.518 --> 00:02:07.153
You think you're going
to win in that game?

00:02:07.153 --> 00:02:08.412
It's not going to happen.

00:02:08.412 --> 00:02:11.408
But you love it, you love the process.

00:02:11.408 --> 00:02:13.756
And so you work harder, and
you continue to practice

00:02:13.756 --> 00:02:15.921
and you get good and you
get better, and you improve,

00:02:15.921 --> 00:02:18.217
and you improve, and you improve.

00:02:18.217 --> 00:02:21.436
And now you're above average,
you're better than good.

00:02:21.436 --> 00:02:23.650
You're starting to get great.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.630
Maybe you're starting to
almost make a full time income

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:26.779
from this thing.

00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:28.969
And people will still look at you,

00:02:28.969 --> 00:02:29.802
you're still doing this?

00:02:29.802 --> 00:02:31.754
Why are you still doing this?

00:02:31.754 --> 00:02:33.696
You spent these years
working on this thing,

00:02:33.696 --> 00:02:35.512
you should've been way
ahead in this other career

00:02:35.512 --> 00:02:37.556
and now you're paying your bills but

00:02:37.556 --> 00:02:39.312
you're never going to be that great thing.

00:02:39.312 --> 00:02:40.151
What do you do?

00:02:40.151 --> 00:02:41.140
You love the process.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.030
You keep working at it,
you keep working at it,

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:45.570
and then you get great,
and then you get amazing,

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:46.870
and then you win.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:50.579
That's the success story for
almost every successful person

00:02:50.579 --> 00:02:51.981
that we've profiled.

00:02:51.981 --> 00:02:53.575
They sucked at the start.

00:02:53.575 --> 00:02:56.654
But they loved the process
and they kept going

00:02:56.654 --> 00:02:58.787
and they improved and they got better.

00:02:58.787 --> 00:03:00.216
That's how you win.

00:03:00.216 --> 00:03:02.250
If you feel this thing inside you

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.045
where you love the process
of doing something.

00:03:05.045 --> 00:03:07.707
Don't be so concerned with
how it's going to work out.

00:03:07.707 --> 00:03:09.788
'Cause quite often the idea
that you have in your head,

00:03:09.788 --> 00:03:11.739
is not how it's going to work out.

00:03:11.739 --> 00:03:13.375
The end result is not what you're chasing,

00:03:13.375 --> 00:03:15.102
the process is what you're chasing.

00:03:15.102 --> 00:03:16.568
When I started this YouTube channel,

00:03:16.568 --> 00:03:18.353
it wasn't to become YouTube famous.

00:03:18.353 --> 00:03:20.304
That wasn't part of my goal.

00:03:20.304 --> 00:03:21.796
I didn't even know how I
was going to ever make money

00:03:21.796 --> 00:03:24.556
off of this, making money
helping entrepreneurs.

00:03:24.556 --> 00:03:26.611
The first thing I did was
three people showed up

00:03:26.611 --> 00:03:27.828
to a free event.

00:03:27.828 --> 00:03:29.496
How are you ever going to
make money off of something

00:03:29.496 --> 00:03:30.928
if you can't get more than three people

00:03:30.928 --> 00:03:33.043
to come to a free event?

00:03:33.043 --> 00:03:34.953
And the world opened up to me in a way

00:03:34.953 --> 00:03:36.578
that I never thought possible.

00:03:36.578 --> 00:03:37.817
I never thought I'd get a book deal

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.057
with Penguin Random House.

00:03:39.057 --> 00:03:40.601
I never thought I'd be asked to join

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:42.905
boards of directors in different companies

00:03:42.905 --> 00:03:44.003
and get paid to do it.

00:03:44.003 --> 00:03:46.005
I never thought I'd work with big brands

00:03:46.005 --> 00:03:49.509
who would then hire me out to
work with them on projects.

00:03:49.509 --> 00:03:51.105
I never thought these things would happen

00:03:51.105 --> 00:03:52.507
and it wasn't even on my radar as

00:03:52.507 --> 00:03:55.055
in my business model or my plan.

00:03:55.055 --> 00:03:57.046
What I wanted to do was
create amazing content

00:03:57.046 --> 00:03:58.387
to help entrepreneurs.

00:03:58.387 --> 00:04:00.083
Helping entrepreneurs feeds my soul

00:04:00.083 --> 00:04:01.325
and I had to find a way to do it

00:04:01.325 --> 00:04:02.889
even if I never made any money.

00:04:02.889 --> 00:04:04.808
And it's because I have
passion and determination

00:04:04.808 --> 00:04:06.689
that I ended up making money.

00:04:06.689 --> 00:04:08.140
That's how it works.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.756
So find the thing that you love doing,

00:04:09.756 --> 00:04:11.666
that you have insane passion towards

00:04:11.666 --> 00:04:14.743
and figure out a way to do
that as much as possible,

00:04:14.743 --> 00:04:16.033
practice as hard as you can

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:18.330
even if you absolutely suck at the start

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:20.206
because that's the thing that's
going to make you come alive.

00:04:20.206 --> 00:04:22.597
That's the thing where you're
going to deliver insane value

00:04:22.597 --> 00:04:24.200
to the world at some point

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.450
when you get really good at it.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:28.031
And the only way to get
there is to practice,

00:04:28.031 --> 00:04:30.712
and practice, and practice,
and practice, and practice

00:04:30.712 --> 00:04:32.907
and stop listening to
the people around you

00:04:32.907 --> 00:04:36.108
who say that you'll never
make it and you can't do it.

00:04:36.108 --> 00:04:39.623
So the question today
guys is what do you love?

00:04:39.623 --> 00:04:41.682
Leave it in the comments,
I'm curious to find out.

00:04:41.682 --> 00:04:43.675
I also want to give a quick
shoutout to James Mitchell.

00:04:43.675 --> 00:04:44.967
James, thank you so much for picking up

00:04:44.967 --> 00:04:46.958
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:04:46.958 --> 00:04:48.195
It really means a lot to me man.

00:04:48.195 --> 00:04:49.497
I appreciate the support

00:04:49.497 --> 00:04:50.908
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:04:50.908 --> 00:04:52.612
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:04:52.612 --> 00:04:53.723
I believe in you.

00:04:53.723 --> 00:04:55.816
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:04:55.816 --> 00:04:58.008
and whatever your one word is.

00:04:58.008 --> 00:05:00.854
Much love and I'll see you
guys again tomorrow morning

00:05:00.854 --> 00:05:03.902
for another Shot of Entspresso.

00:05:03.902 --> 00:05:06.744
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:06.744 --> 00:05:10.327
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:14.650
- Statistics said if I did that

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:16.337
and I stopped going to school

00:05:16.337 --> 00:05:18.265
and that's all I did was hang in the hood,

00:05:18.265 --> 00:05:20.551
then I wasn't going to be here today.

00:05:20.551 --> 00:05:22.624
So that's why I still
hang with the same people

00:05:22.624 --> 00:05:24.412
that I was with back in the hood

00:05:24.412 --> 00:05:26.008
and I changed my mentality.

00:05:26.008 --> 00:05:28.629
I don't think the same way
I was when I was there.

00:05:28.629 --> 00:05:30.925
I opened my mind up, I thought broader,

00:05:30.925 --> 00:05:32.631
I thought outside of my horizons.

00:05:32.631 --> 00:05:34.338
And like you got to think outside the box

00:05:34.338 --> 00:05:36.968
because that's the only way
you're going to get out.

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:37.963
When you're trapped in the trap,

00:05:37.963 --> 00:05:40.230
you're really mentally
trapped in the trap.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:43.095
And it's me like man, I
want to make sure my people

00:05:43.095 --> 00:05:46.772
just know that that's just
not the end of your life.

00:05:46.772 --> 00:05:48.671
Like if somebody tells
you, these statistics,

00:05:48.671 --> 00:05:49.556
this is not you.

00:05:49.556 --> 00:05:51.840
You're going to fight statistics
and go to the next level.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.802
Like statistics said I
wouldn't even be here

00:05:53.802 --> 00:05:56.484
talking to you right now,
if I were to listen to them

00:05:56.484 --> 00:05:58.522
and tell them how my life
how my life would've been.

00:05:58.522 --> 00:06:01.125
They say one out of ten people,
they're going to be like this

00:06:01.125 --> 00:06:03.514
or nine out of ten Black
males, if they do this,

00:06:03.514 --> 00:06:05.972
live this way, they're going to do this.

00:06:05.972 --> 00:06:06.805
You know what I'm saying?

00:06:06.805 --> 00:06:07.902
There's no way around it.

00:06:07.902 --> 00:06:10.788
They're going to tell you
there's no way around it.

00:06:10.788 --> 00:06:12.117
So if you're in the hood right now,

00:06:12.117 --> 00:06:14.311
you're standing on the block everyday.

00:06:14.311 --> 00:06:16.109
The police just riding by that old lady

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:19.471
that's looking at you, just
calling the police on you.

00:06:19.471 --> 00:06:20.955
The people who're riding
by just looking at you

00:06:20.955 --> 00:06:21.951
like they ain't nothing.

00:06:21.951 --> 00:06:22.784
Your parents saying it,

00:06:22.784 --> 00:06:24.563
they think you ain't
never going to be nothing,

00:06:24.563 --> 00:06:25.944
they think you're going to be like that

00:06:25.944 --> 00:06:27.373
for the rest of your life.

00:06:27.373 --> 00:06:29.317
Who is the person to tell you

00:06:29.317 --> 00:06:31.540
that you're going to be
standing on this block

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:32.536
all your life?

00:06:32.536 --> 00:06:33.889
It's supposed to be a point in your life

00:06:33.889 --> 00:06:37.006
where you only be here for, you
give yourself a year or two.

00:06:37.006 --> 00:06:39.435
You're from here, it don't do no good

00:06:39.435 --> 00:06:41.364
for you to be here all your life.

00:06:41.364 --> 00:06:43.650
And you spending the
majority of your life,

00:06:43.650 --> 00:06:47.449
22 hours out of your day, trying to prove

00:06:47.449 --> 00:06:48.861
you're the hardest in the hood.

00:06:48.861 --> 00:06:50.529
You come from this, you were born in this.

00:06:50.529 --> 00:06:52.163
When you came home from the hospital,

00:06:52.163 --> 00:06:54.133
you went to the hood.

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:54.966
You know what I'm saying?

00:06:54.966 --> 00:06:56.571
So you don't live your whole life this way

00:06:56.571 --> 00:06:57.404
for all your life.

00:06:57.404 --> 00:07:00.107
You deserve to live in a
different neighborhood,

00:07:00.107 --> 00:07:01.549
to better yourself for three, four years

00:07:01.549 --> 00:07:03.349
out of your whole life, when
you've been living this way

00:07:03.349 --> 00:07:05.349
probably, some dudes been living that way

00:07:05.349 --> 00:07:07.778
for 20 years, 23 years.

00:07:07.778 --> 00:07:10.509
Been in the hood since they
came home from the hospital

00:07:10.509 --> 00:07:13.534
and they're still trying
to prove to the hood

00:07:13.534 --> 00:07:16.419
how hard they are and
they end up not making it.

00:07:16.419 --> 00:07:17.783
Because they didn't prove to themselves,

00:07:17.783 --> 00:07:20.009
you got to prove to
yourself that you want more

00:07:20.009 --> 00:07:22.000
than what the hood has to offer.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.980
At the end of the day, from my first song,

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:25.005
when I first made it my head.

00:07:25.005 --> 00:07:26.508
I knew what I could do,
you know what I'm saying?

00:07:26.508 --> 00:07:27.982
I know the type of artist that I am,

00:07:27.982 --> 00:07:31.834
I know the caliber of
music that I can come with

00:07:31.834 --> 00:07:33.102
and I know I can continue to do it.

00:07:33.102 --> 00:07:34.240
I was born to make music

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:35.571
and when you got a gift for something,

00:07:35.571 --> 00:07:37.624
you just got to know how to utilize it.

00:07:37.624 --> 00:07:39.177
And when I found a way to utilize it

00:07:39.177 --> 00:07:41.383
and just make the most of my opportunity,

00:07:41.383 --> 00:07:42.550
I know I have to be...

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:43.902
I'm an artist, I have
to stay in the studio

00:07:43.902 --> 00:07:45.934
and create all the time,
you know what I'm saying?

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:47.841
If I was to lay off and
not go to the studio,

00:07:47.841 --> 00:07:50.552
then all those he say, she says,

00:07:50.552 --> 00:07:52.160
it might've came true,

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:54.183
but I knew the work that I was putting in.

00:07:54.183 --> 00:07:57.138
The key to success is like,

00:07:57.138 --> 00:07:59.242
when you haven't been successful

00:07:59.242 --> 00:08:00.786
you don't know what's the key to success,

00:08:00.786 --> 00:08:02.237
how to be successful.

00:08:02.237 --> 00:08:04.078
You know the right
moves that you're making

00:08:04.078 --> 00:08:05.924
and every move that you're
making and you're striving

00:08:05.924 --> 00:08:07.520
and you're just achieving certain things

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:09.562
that you made goals for yourself.

00:08:09.562 --> 00:08:11.168
You set goals and you achieve goals

00:08:11.168 --> 00:08:12.001
but at the end of the day,

00:08:12.001 --> 00:08:14.367
you still set your standards high.

00:08:14.367 --> 00:08:15.780
For when you reach a certain plateau

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:18.221
and then you know man, I got
to go to that next level,

00:08:18.221 --> 00:08:19.452
you know what I'm saying?

00:08:19.452 --> 00:08:20.590
When you want to be successful, like,

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:22.499
success is different for other people,

00:08:22.499 --> 00:08:24.249
you know what I mean?

00:08:25.165 --> 00:08:28.245
Success for me is just making music

00:08:28.245 --> 00:08:31.895
and that's being successful is just

00:08:31.895 --> 00:08:33.274
winning a Grammy,

00:08:33.274 --> 00:08:34.550
you know what I mean?

